<div class="lede">
  <p><strong>The short version.</strong> SpotOn is a marketplace: it connects people who need to park with people who have a private space to rent out. By creating an account you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <p>We take a service fee out of every booking — 15% on hourly and daily stays, 7% on weekly and monthly stays — and the rest goes to the host through Stripe. You must be 18 or older to use SpotOn, because using it means entering into a payment transaction.</p>
  <p>No abuse, harassment or objectionable content. Report or block anyone who breaks this, and we act within 24 hours.</p>
  <p>The rest of this page is the detail behind those sentences.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="who"><span class="num">01</span>Who we are</h2>
<p>SpotOn is a mobile app for renting private parking spaces, published by Ehan Shah, based in Gainesville, Florida ("we", "us", "SpotOn"). These terms cover the SpotOn iOS and Android apps and the servers behind them. They govern the relationship between you and SpotOn — not whatever a renter and a host separately agree between themselves off the platform.</p>
<p>SpotOn is a venue, not a party to any parking arrangement. We don't own the parking spaces listed, and we're not the one parking your car.</p>

<h2 id="eligibility"><span class="num">02</span>Eligibility and accounts</h2>
<p>You must be 18 or older to create an account. You're responsible for keeping your login credentials to yourself and for everything that happens under your account. Tell us at <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a> if you think someone else has access to it.</p>
<p>The information you give us at sign-up and afterwards — your name, your vehicle details, your listings — needs to be accurate. Listing a space you don't have the right to rent out, or registering a vehicle or plate that isn't yours, breaks these terms.</p>

<h2 id="listing"><span class="num">03</span>Listing a space</h2>
<p>If you list a space, you're confirming that you have the legal right to offer it for parking — as the owner, or with the owner's permission — and that the address, photos, price and availability you post are accurate. A listing is public inside the app: anyone searching can see its address, position on the map and photos.</p>
<p>You're responsible for honoring a confirmed booking. If a renter shows up to a space that isn't available as listed, the renter is refunded as described in <a href="#cancellations">§6</a>, and repeated failures to honor bookings can lead to suspension under <a href="#termination">§10</a>.</p>

<h2 id="booking"><span class="num">04</span>Booking a space</h2>
<p>When you book, you're agreeing to park only the vehicle you registered for that booking, only for the window you paid for, and only in the space as described. While a booking is active, the host can see your vehicle's full license plate — see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for exactly how that works.</p>
<p>SpotOn does not inspect, verify or guarantee any listed space beyond what the host tells us. Check the listing details and photos before you book.</p>

<h2 id="fees"><span class="num">05</span>Fees and payments</h2>
<p>Payment runs through Stripe. Your card is charged the listing's rate plus our service fee at the time of booking; card details go straight to Stripe and never reach our servers.</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Stay length</th><th>Service fee</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Hourly or daily</td><td>15% of the booking subtotal</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Weekly or monthly</td><td>7% of the booking subtotal</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p>The remainder — the host's payout — is transferred to the host's Stripe-connected account. Hosts go through Stripe's own identity verification before they can receive payouts; SpotOn never holds or has access to the funds in between.</p>

<h2 id="cancellations"><span class="num">06</span>Cancellations and refunds</h2>
<p>You can cancel a confirmed booking yourself from the app, for a full refund including the service fee, up until 24 hours before it's scheduled to start. We reserve the right to change that window going forward; the number in effect at the time you book is the one that applies to that booking.</p>
<p>Once you're inside that window, or after a booking has started, self-serve cancellation isn't available. Email <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a> and we'll look at it case by case.</p>
<p>One case is automatic on our end: if a host never finishes Stripe onboarding in time to receive a booking's payout, we automatically refund the renter in full and cancel the booking.</p>
<h3>If the space isn't available when you arrive</h3>
<p>If you arrive and the space is unavailable, blocked, or the host refuses you access, email <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a> within 24 hours of the booking's start time, ideally with a photo. We'll review it, and if we confirm the problem, we'll refund you in full and withhold the host's payout for that booking.</p>

<h3>If you don't show up</h3>
<p>A booking reserves the space for you for the whole window you paid for, so the host can't rent it to anyone else. If you don't show up, or don't use the full window, you won't be refunded once you're inside the 24-hour cancellation window.</p>

<h3>If a host cancels</h3>
<p>Hosts shouldn't cancel confirmed bookings. If a host has to, the renter gets a full refund. Repeated host cancellations can lead to the host's listings being removed or their account being suspended.</p>

<h2 id="conduct"><span class="num">07</span>Acceptable use</h2>
<p>Don't use SpotOn to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>List a space you don't have the right to offer, or park in a space you haven't booked</li>
  <li>Provide false information about your identity, your vehicle, or a listing</li>
  <li>Harass, threaten, or attempt to defraud another user</li>
  <li>Circumvent SpotOn's payment system to pay or be paid outside the app for a booking arranged through it</li>
  <li>Interfere with or attempt to reverse-engineer the app or its backend</li>
</ul>
<p>We can remove a listing, cancel a booking, or suspend an account that breaks these rules — see <a href="#termination">§10</a>.</p>

<h2 id="content"><span class="num">08</span>User content, reporting and blocking</h2>
<p>"User content" means anything you put into SpotOn: your listings (including photos, descriptions and addresses), the messages you send, and your profile information. You keep ownership of your content. By posting it, you give SpotOn a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to host, store, display and share it inside the app as needed to run the service — for example, showing your listing to people searching, or delivering your messages. That license ends when you delete the content or your account, except for copies we need to keep as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h3>Zero tolerance</h3>
<p>SpotOn has zero tolerance for objectionable content and abusive users. Don't post or send anything that is:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Harassment, bullying, or threats</li>
  <li>Hate speech, or content that attacks people based on who they are</li>
  <li>Sexual or sexually explicit content</li>
  <li>Scams, fraud, or attempts to mislead other users</li>
  <li>Spam or unsolicited advertising</li>
  <li>Illegal, or infringing someone else's rights, including their privacy, copyright or trademarks</li>
</ul>

<h3>Reporting</h3>
<p>If someone breaks these rules, tell us. You can report a user from your chat with them, or report a listing from its details page, right in the app. You can also email <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a>. Reports go to the SpotOn team.</p>

<h3>Blocking</h3>
<p>You can block another user in the app. Once you block someone, they can no longer message you, and your conversation with them is hidden.</p>

<h3>What we do about it</h3>
<p>We review reports within 24 hours. Where content breaks these terms, we'll remove it, and where appropriate we'll suspend or permanently ban the user responsible — see <a href="#termination">§10</a>.</p>

<h2 id="disclaimer"><span class="num">09</span>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
<p>SpotOn connects renters and hosts; it does not itself provide parking, and we don't guarantee a listed space will be available, safe, or as described.</p>

<h3>The app is provided "as is"</h3>
<p>SpotOn is provided "as is" and "as available". To the fullest extent the law allows, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title and non-infringement, and any warranty that the app will be uninterrupted, error-free or secure.</p>

<h3>Parking is at your own risk</h3>
<p>You park in a host's space at your own risk. SpotOn isn't responsible for loss of or damage to vehicles or other property, or for personal injury, that happens in or around a listed space. Hosts are responsible for their own space — its condition, its safety, and having any insurance they need — and renters are responsible for their own vehicle and belongings.</p>

<h3>Limits on our liability</h3>
<p>To the fullest extent the law allows, SpotOn won't be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue or data, arising out of or relating to these terms or the app, even if we've been told they're possible.</p>
<p>Our total liability to you for any claim arising out of or relating to these terms or the app is limited to the greater of (a) the service fees SpotOn received from you in the 12 months before the claim arose, or (b) $100.</p>
<p>Some jurisdictions don't allow certain warranties to be disclaimed or certain damages to be limited, so some of the above may not apply to you. Nothing in these terms is meant to limit any right you have that can't be limited under Florida or federal law.</p>

<h3>Indemnification</h3>
<p>You agree to defend, indemnify and hold harmless SpotOn and Ehan Shah from any claims, losses, damages, liabilities and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of your listings, your bookings, your user content, or your breach of these terms or the law.</p>

<h2 id="termination"><span class="num">10</span>Suspension and termination</h2>
<p>You can delete your account at any time from Profile in the app — see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> §8 for exactly what that does. We can suspend or terminate an account that breaks these terms, with notice where practical. If you have a booking or payout in progress, see the deletion-timing rules in the Privacy Policy — the same reasoning applies to suspension.</p>

<h2 id="disputes"><span class="num">11</span>Disputes and governing law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, United States, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.</p>

<h3>Let's talk first</h3>
<p>Before either of us starts an arbitration or a lawsuit, email <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a> describing the dispute and what you're asking for. We'll spend 30 days trying to resolve it directly before either of us files anything.</p>

<h3>Binding individual arbitration</h3>
<p>If that doesn't resolve things, you and SpotOn agree that any dispute arising out of or relating to these terms or the app will be resolved by binding arbitration administered by the American Arbitration Association under its Consumer Arbitration Rules, rather than in court — except that either of us may bring an individual claim in small claims court instead, and either of us may seek injunctive relief in court to stop unauthorized use of our intellectual property or the platform. Arbitration will take place in Alachua County, Florida, or be conducted by phone, video, or on written submissions if the arbitrator agrees. The arbitrator, not any court, decides any dispute about the interpretation or enforceability of this section — except for the class-action waiver below, which only a court can decide.</p>
<p>If your claim is $10,000 or less, we will pay any arbitration fees beyond what AAA's Consumer Arbitration Rules already reduce for individual filers, unless the arbitrator finds your claim frivolous.</p>

<h3>No class actions</h3>
<p>You and SpotOn each agree to bring any dispute in arbitration on an individual basis only, not as a plaintiff or class member in any purported class, consolidated, or representative action, and the arbitrator cannot preside over any such proceeding or combine more than one person's claims. If this class-action waiver is found unenforceable as to a particular claim or request for relief, that claim or request must be brought in court instead, and this section still applies to every other claim.</p>

<h3>Opting out</h3>
<p>You can opt out of this arbitration agreement — everything else in these terms still applies — by emailing <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a> within 30 days of creating your account, from the email address on the account, stating that you want to opt out of arbitration. If you opt out, disputes between you and SpotOn go to the state or federal courts located in Alachua County, Florida, and you and SpotOn each waive any right to a jury trial.</p>

<h2 id="changes"><span class="num">12</span>Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>If we change these terms, we'll update the date at the top, and for anything significant we'll tell you in the app before it takes effect. Continuing to use SpotOn after a change means you accept the new terms.</p>

<h2 id="contact"><span class="num">13</span>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about these terms, or anything here that doesn't match what you see in the app: <a href="mailto:team.spotonapp@gmail.com">team.spotonapp@gmail.com</a>.</p>

